#
# /etc/default/jack, read by jackd-cuems.service. The package copies this file
# there only when it is missing; after that the file belongs to the box and no
# upgrade touches it.
#
# Default: the internal analog output. "Analog" is the ALSA id the platform
# profile gives that card on every platform. For another device (a USB
# interface, the HDMI outputs as multi_hdmi) edit the -d argument.
# jackd-cuems.service sets the user; do not add a USER= line.

DAEMON_ARGS="-R -dalsa -dhw:Analog,0 -r48000 -p512 -n3"
